<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2022/05/microsoft-edge-hero.jpg" alt="" width="160" height="90" class="alignleft size-full wp-image-1058944"" />Microsoft is testing support for signing into its <a href="https://explore.microsoft.com/en-us/edge">Edge</a> browser using your Apple Account, avoiding the need to create a Microsoft account. Two new flags related to the support were spotted by <em><a href="https://macmagazine.com.br/post/2026/08/11/microsoft-edge-permitira-fazer-login-diretamente-com-uma-conta-apple/">MacMagazine</a></em> in the latest Edge Canary build, with the feature also rolling out to Edge Beta users.<br/>
<br/>
One of the flags enables Apple Account sign-in for Edge profiles, while the other adds an Apple sign-in button to the profile menu (where a Google Account sign-in option already exists). In its <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/deployedge/microsoft-edge-relnote-beta-channel">release notes</a> for Edge Beta 152, Microsoft already lists Apple Account sign-in support for Windows and macOS, but describes it as a "controlled rollout," so there may be some delay before all beta users see it.<div class="linkback">Tag: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/microsoft-edge/">Microsoft Edge</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/12/microsoft-edge-browser-apple-account-sign-in/">Microsoft Edge Browser to Get Apple Account Sign-In Support</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/microsoft-edge-browser-to-get-apple-account-sign-in-support.2486809/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>